branch: feature/retry-js
worktree: ../okay-wt-retry
spec: specs/parallel-resilience.md (retry's law, to be extended) — BACKLOG entry

why: `okay.retry` (src/main/scala-jvm-native/Parallel.scala) reruns a
  program by `prog.runWith` in a try/catch with Thread.sleep between
  attempts — a parking road that JS cannot have, so JS has no retry.
what: `retryAsync(policy)(prog): A ! Async` in the shared core — an
  Async PROGRAM: Async.attempt for the failure as data, Async.sleep for
  the delay, the policy exhausted re-raises the last error. Laws in
  the cross suite (JVM, JS, Native): retries per the policy, succeeds
  when an attempt succeeds, rethrows the LAST error when exhausted,
  delays are honoured (elapsed >= sum), zero-delay policy does not
  sleep. The blocking `retry` stays as it is.
